> How would I test strong invariance for ordinal variables? Could you give an example?

There is an example with 5-category Likert-type indicators here:

http://www.myweb.ttu.edu/spornpra/catInvariance.html

> if its the regression path I should worry about, measurement invariance isn't required as an assumption?

Yes, weak invariance across groups is necessary to compare latent regression slopes across those groups.  And strong invariance would be necessary to compare latent means across groups.

Terry

