Anna--
     You used the cfa function, which imposes more defaults than the lavaan function.  The lavaan.pdf documentation available online (search using www.rseek.org <http://www.rseek.org>) specifies (p. 9)

"Details

The cfa function is a wrapper for the more general lavaan function, using the following default
arguments: int.ov.free = TRUE, int.lv.free = FALSE, auto.fix.first = TRUE (unless
std.lv <http://std.lv> = TRUE), auto.fix.single = TRUE, auto.var = TRUE, auto.cov.lv.x = TRUE,
auto.th <http://auto.th> = TRUE, auto.delta = TRUE, and auto.cov.y = TRUE."

To see the difference, run the same model using the lavaan function.  You will get as many error and warning messages as you wish.
--Ed Rigdon

