> Is there an R package that can do simultaneous regression equations such
> that I can determine how well each IV predicts each DV (classic
> "horizontal" comparisons) and that allows me to assess each IVs
> differential influence on each DV ("vertical" comparisons)?

Yes. If you treat everything as continuous. lavaan is one package. There
are others. But see below.

> S2 	count
> S3 	count
> E1 	count
> E2 	count
> E3 	count
> E4 	count

lavaan (0.5-18) has no support for 'count' data.

> If R cannot do this analysis but Mplus can, can someone please explain
> what it is about Mplus that allows it to do what R cannot?

Mplus does handle count data (and zero-inflated count data).

Yves.

